-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over q for the two fibre components
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and write $\mathcal O' =$ `IgusaScheme.chartAlgInf (N₀ * q) q` for the pole chart subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $N_0q$ over the base ring `DRLevel.R q`, and `chartAlgFin` for the corresponding $j$-finite chart. The data are: an automorphism $w$ of the scheme `DRLevel.X N₀ q` with $w \circ$ `toBase` $=$ `toBase` (so $w$ is over the base, where `toBase` is `IgusaScheme.igusaTo (N₀ * q) q`); an `R q`-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of `chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` which, after inclusion into the modular function field, agrees with `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N₀ q` (the automorphism chosen by `IsAtkinLehnerAutFull`, or the identity if none exists); the hypothesis that `ιFin (N₀ * q) q` followed by $w$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\theta)$ followed by `ιFin (N₀ * q) q`; a morphism $\pi :$ `X N₀ q` $\to$ `X0 N₀ q` with $\pi \circ$ `toBase0` $=$ `toBase`; an `R q`-algebra map $\iota_0 :$ `chartAlgFin N₀ q` $\to$ `chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` preserving Laurent expansions over $\mathbb Q$, with `ιFin (N₀ * q) q` followed by $\pi$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_0)$ followed by `ιFin N₀ q`; an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$ that is an `R q`-algebra; a morphism $c'$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R q} \mathcal O')$ to the fibre $\mathfrak X_\kappa =$ `pullback (toBase N₀ q) (Spec.map (algebraMap (R q) κ))` whose two components are $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion followed by `ιInf (N₀ * q) q`, and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion $\kappa \to \kappa \otimes_{R q} \mathcal O'$; and two morphisms $\mathrm{comp}_0, \mathrm{comp}_1$ from the fibre $(\mathfrak X_0)_\kappa$ of `toBase0` to $\mathfrak X_\kappa$, each over $\kappa$ (compatible with the second pullback projections) and a closed immersion, with $\mathrm{comp}_0$ followed by `fibreMap0 π` the identity and $\mathrm{comp}_0$ followed by `fibreMap w.hom` equal to $\mathrm{comp}_1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of ideals $P_0, P_1$ of $\mathcal O'$, each a minimal prime of the ideal generated by $q$, with $P_0 \ne P_1$, such that for $i \in \{0,1\}$ and every point $z$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R q} \mathcal O')$ whose image under $c'$ lies in the set-theoretic image of $\mathrm{comp}_i$, the ideal generated by the image of $P_i$ under the right inclusion $\mathcal O' \to \kappa \otimes_{R q} \mathcal O'$ is contained in the prime ideal of $z$.
--
--   This records, in the coordinates of the pole chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes \mathcal O')$, that the two copies of the level-$N_0$ fibre inside the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the model of $X_0(N_0q)$ — one split off by the forgetful map $\pi$, the other its translate by the Atkin–Lehner automorphism — lie over two distinct minimal primes of $q\mathcal O'$, i.e. on two distinct irreducible components of the special fibre, as in the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction of $X_0(N_0q)$ at $q$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin).
